Sorry mate but to me this idea sucks oozing drek, aside from turning
archeologists (sp?) into the only effective spellcasters it's also
counterintuative, obscure and hard to play.

Consider, you have a spellbook of fireball (or whatever) and don't find
any of the right gems, hell how do you even know WHICH are the right
gems, there is no way I'm gonna test fire a spell just to see if I've
got the proper rock this time.

Gems are rare and valuable, to make this work they would have to be
common and dirt cheap, thus people would carry sacks of them and have
max luck at all times from playing catch with unicorns

NH3.11 handles spells pretty well (IMO), personaly the only problem
I have with the magic system is the way casting a spell takes both
food AND spell points, very greedy I think...

Perhaps casting a spell takes magic points and gaining magic points
back costs food, that way at lesat the drain is more spread and you
don't faint with hunger from casting detect food..


